          deckDescription: 'One or more standard 52-card decks; each has four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs) and thirteen ranks. No jokers; multiple decks are often shuffled together. Only the point value of each card matters for the total.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits are irrelevant in blackjack; only the numeric value of the card (ace one or eleven, face cards ten, others face value) is used to compute the hand total.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit: aces count one or eleven, kings queens and jacks count ten, two through ten count face value. The object is to reach a total of twenty-one or as close as possible without exceeding it.',
          dealPattern: 'Individually clockwise starting from left of dealer.',
          bettingLimits: 'Fixed Limit',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; cumulative card point total determines strength.',
          rankingSystem: 'Point Total (21 High)',
